This repository is under more than one licence. Which one applies depends on
which directory a file is in.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  julia/                      GNU General Public License v3.0 or later
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Julia implementation in julia/ derives from Sai Koukuntla's DLDS package
(https://github.com/saikoukunt/dLDS), released by him under GPL v3. Because it
is a derivative of GPL-licensed code, julia/ is GPL v3 or later; this is not a
choice we could make differently. The full licence text is in julia/LICENSE, and
every file in julia/src/ carries a header recording its provenance and, where it
was modified, what changed and why.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  everything else (MIT)       analysis/ features/ figures/ dlds_release/ and root
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python code never loads the Julia code. The two halves communicate only
through .npy files on disk, so they are separate programs distributed together,
which section 5 of the GPL explicitly permits ("mere aggregation"). The GPL's
copyleft therefore does not reach this code.

